# Nobody's things in Russian: ничей, ничто, кто-либо
subtitle: "Чьи это вещи? — Ничьи. Ничто не помешает, ни с кем, кто-либо: the ни- family and official -либо, as an inspector checks the kitchen of «Кухонька»."
tags: ["russian","ничей","ничто","кто-либо","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/negatives","grammar/indefinite-pronouns"]
thumb: "band \"Nobody's things in Russian\" stamp \"НИЧЕЙ\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Made by the chef in Russian: составлено, печётся, открыли","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/213-russian-passive-in-full.cast"}

## Nobody's things in Russian: ничей, ничто, кто-либо
